Reason:
The `isAlive()` method only exists in JDK8 and leads to compatibility issues in earlier Java versions, causing potential runtime exceptions when checking if a process is alive.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```java
private boolean isAlive(Process p) {
    try {
        p.exitValue();
        return false;
    } catch (IllegalThreadStateException e) {
        return true;
    }
}
```
Reason:
This custom `isAlive()` method provides a compatible alternative to check the process status by using `exitValue()`, which is available in earlier Java versions, thus avoiding runtime exceptions and maintaining compatibility.

